# Lefty's Voice — settings. Copy to .env and edit. Never commit your .env.
#
# EVERY VALUE NEEDS QUOTES. An unquoted device name with a space in it killed
# the whole launcher on 2026-09-22 and took a while to find. Quote everything,
# even when it looks like it does not need them.

# ── Audio devices ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave both commented out to use whatever your system already defaults to.
# That is the right answer for almost everyone. Set them only if you have more
# than one microphone or speaker and the wrong one gets picked.
#
# The exact names come from your OS sound settings.
#VOICE_INPUT_DEVICE="Your Microphone Name"
#VOICE_OUTPUT_DEVICE="Your Speaker Name"

# How much audio to hold while you talk. Raise it only if long sentences get
# cut off.
#VOICE_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE="500"

# ── Optional: ElevenLabs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lefty speaks through Kokoro by default, which runs on your machine, costs
# nothing, and needs no account. ElevenLabs is an optional upgrade with a nicer
# voice and a bill attached.
#
# Leave these empty unless you actually want it. Put the real key in .env only
# -- never in .env.example, never in a commit, never in a note.
#ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=""
#ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=""

# ── Where Lefty's memory lives ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Notes inside this folder are exempt from the spoken approval gate, because
# writing its own memory is the job. Everything outside it still has to ask.
#LEFTY_MEMORY_DIR="$HOME/lefty/lefty-in-a-box/memory"
